      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load data (float32, 8000 x 1024) -- ~31.25 MiB in memory\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy')\n    N, D = X.shape\n\n    # Precompute squared norms of each row (float64 for accuracy)\n    norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total_upper = 0.0  # sum over i < j of distances\n\n    block_size = 500  # tuned to keep memory usage low\n\n    for a in range(0, N, block_size):\n        end_i = min(a + block_size, N)\n        bi = end_i - a\n        Xi = X[a:end_i]          # shape (bi, D)\n        Xj = X[a:N]              # shape (bj, D)\n        bj = N - a\n\n        # Dot products between rows in this block and all rows from a onward\n        dot = Xi @ Xj.T          # (bi, bj), float32\n\n        ni = norms[a:end_i][:, None]     # (bi,1) float64\n        nj = norms[a:N][None, :]         # (1,bj) float64\n\n        # Squared distances (float64 for numerical stability)\n        sq = ni + nj - 2.0 * dot.astype(np.float64)\n        np.maximum(sq, 0.0, out=sq)\n        d = np.sqrt(sq)\n\n        # Build mask for strictly upper part: global j > global i\n        # local row r -> global i = a + r\n        # local col c -> global j = a + c\n        rows = np.arange(bi)[:, None]\n        cols = np.arange(bj)[None, :]\n        mask = cols > rows\n\n        total_upper += d[mask].sum(dtype=np.float64)\n\n        # free memory explicitly\n        del dot, sq, d, mask, ni, nj\n\n    total = 2.0 * total_upper\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.6f}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
